  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale:\nThe central idea is to optimize the step function by: 1) Upsampling the initial solution to higher densities to resolve finer details, and 2) Applying local optimization at each resolution level. This hierarchical approach leverages resolution transfer from sparse to dense grids while ensuring integral preservation. The key bottleneck addressed is the combinatorial explosion in grid size that limits direct optimization at high resolutions. This method balances exploration (via upsampled transitions) with refinement (via concentrated iterations at chosen densities).\n\n2. Mathematical Specification:\n- Representation: Discrete n-point samples with dx=2.0/n over [0,2]\n- Objective: min max_k(\u222bh(x)(1-h(x+k))dx) using np.correlate(mode='full')*dx\n- Constraints:\n  - 0\u2264h[i]\u22641 for all i\n  - \u2211h[i] = n/2 exactly  \n- Resolution transfer: Upholding integral preservation via np.repeat for upsample and uniform averaging for downsample\n- Optimization: CVXPY with exponential cone programming to handle inherent curvature while respecting 0/1 values and sum constraint\n\n3. Implementation Procedure:\nParent solution validation:\n- Verify initial_h satisfies 0\u2264initial_h[i]\u22641 and \u2211h[i]=35\n- If invalid, repair by proportional scaling\nHierarchical optimization pipeline:\n- Upsample resolution factor 2 to 140 (dx halved) preserving integral\n- Perform 2 iterations at 140 via:\n  Primary: CVXPY ex con solver\n  Secondary: LBFGS-B constrained minimization\n- Evaluate using np.correlate() at 140 for score\nParallel exploration at 70/140:\n- Generate 3 random solutions at 70 meeting sum constraint\n- Perform minimization with 10 points of initial simplex\nLocal refinement strategy:\n- Count minutes: 1st 30m for 70-grid\n  - Spend 20m for CD optimization\n  - Spend 10m for local targeting\nNext level preparation:\n- Densify to 280 via np.repeat\n- Maintain integral via uniform scaling\n- Deploy for surveillance runs in subsequent phase\n\n4. Search Choices and Variations:\nPrimary resolution: 140 points (for most intensive phase)\nSecondary: 70-point baseline\nMutation: Simpson's rule-inspired perturbations (undirected)\nTransfer scaling: integral preservation factor 0.75 (from 200ms testing)\nSolver: CVXPY with ECO solver parameters: {targeting': True, 'scale': 1.0, 'kappa': 1e-3}\n\n5. Budget and Robustness:\nDominant cost: 140-grid evaluations O(140^2)=19.6k per run\nTime estimates: 10m for 70-grid\u2060 \u00b7 70m for 140-grid\u2060 \u00b7 70m for downtime\nDenser grids: 50 survivors at 30-second maximum\nTimeout recovery: Revert to best_last at 1h warning\nConstraint handling: CVXPY's auto-scaling with expansion\nRepair logic: Rejection until integral\u224835 (error bound \u00b10.05)\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract:\n- Verify final h satisfies 0\u2264h[i]\u22641, \u2211h[i]=n/2\n- Compute C5 = np.max(np.correlate(h,1-h,'full'))*dx\n- Sanity checks: Minimal score per resolution via dual-grid consistency\n- Final report structure: (h_values, c5_bound, n_points) with annotated times\n- Maintain design via interpolation: np.repeat/downsample for cross-resolution",
